Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:22:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): count against messages in scope, not every
 record loaded

"Showing 17 of 500 MARADMINs" put the filtered count against every MARADMIN
held in memory, so the line contradicted the date range printed directly
beneath it and the All Messages tab reading 18. The filter itself was always
correct: with This Week active, currentMessages was 17 and exactly 17 cards
rendered, every one inside the window.

The denominator is now every message surviving the filters in force, which is
the same number the All Messages tab shows. That MARADMIN view now reads
"Showing 17 of 18 messages from the last 7 days".

- Add allFeedMessages() and countInScope(), one implementation feeding the
  status line, the Summary Overview, and every tab counter, so the numbers on
  screen cannot disagree.
- updateTabCounters delegates to countInScope instead of duplicating the
  date and search logic.
- The status line names the window when a date filter is active, and appends
  matching "term" when a search is active.
- Summary Overview's Total Showing uses the same denominator.
- Bump app.js cache buster to v=41.

Verified in headless Chromium against a stubbed proxy. In every case the
denominator equals the All Messages tab count: NAVMC under All gives "824 of
1332", NAVMC under 180 Days gives "118 of 133 messages from the last 180
days", the All tab under 180 Days gives "all 133", and an empty window gives
"Showing 0 messages from the last 7 days". Zero empty cards throughout, and
ESLint holds at main's 37-warning baseline with no errors.

