From 910087fc4e1098b3502e98e057102d12de980ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:39:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(cmr): add Court-Martial Reports as a static data
 type

Adds the monthly Marine Corps General and Special Court-Martial dispositions
listing from sja.marines.mil, built on the FA checklist pattern: a script
generates a committed data file, and the app reads it at load with no runtime
network call, so the tab renders even with the proxy down.

Data:
- lib/court-martial-data.js carries 113 monthly reports covering January 2017
  through May 2026, with no gaps in the archive.
- Each record links directly to that month's PDF on media.defense.gov rather
  than to the listing page.
- The listing also publishes JAGINST enclosures and reference PDFs. Those are a
  different kind of document and are excluded, matched by title shape.

Script:
- scripts/fetch-court-martial.mjs, wired to npm run fetch-cmr.
- Discovers the pagination parameter from the markup instead of hard-coding
  smdpage162653, which is a site-generated module id.
- Matches rows by title shape rather than table class, verified against the
  live DOM: 15 rows on page 1, 9 pages, every date and description found.
- Re-encodes media.defense.gov paths, which carry spaces and parentheses.
- Refuses to write an empty file or one under 80 percent of the committed
  record count, leaving existing data in place and exiting non-zero. The FA
  script writes an empty file on failure, which turns one bad network run into
  a silent deletion of the archive.
- Must run from a workstation. sja.marines.mil returns HTTP 403 to datacenter
  ranges including GitHub Actions runners, the same restriction the FA workflow
  already documents.

App wiring: state array, loader, filter branch, All Messages aggregation, tab
counter, badge label and scarlet badge style, message template, and the tab
button. No CSP change is needed, since the PDF links are navigations rather
than fetches. Cache busters move to app.js?v=42 and style.css?v=33.

Verified in headless Chromium: 113 records load, the tab counter reads 113,
113 cards render with zero empty, the first card deep-links to the May 2026
PDF with correct percent-encoding, searching "2023 october" narrows to 1, the
180-day range gives 2 of 136, and the All tab shows both CMR cards among 136.
No page errors, and ESLint holds at main's 37-warning baseline with no errors.

